"smart_blocks:Computer Science/C++/C++ - Random number generation.md#FF5582A6;\">poor statistical properties, limited range, and is not thread-safe</mark>. The ==modern C++ <\\random> library (introduced in C++11) solves these problems== by providing a powerful, flexible, and high-quality framework for generating random numbers. It separates the concerns of raw number generation (engines) from the shaping of those numbers into specific statistical distributions, giving developers fine-grained control and producing much higher-quality random results.": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.08530612,-0.05341053,-0.01941922,-0.02057323,-0.01980706,0.02398356,-0.11232587,0.01271581,0.0613038,0.00170109,0.03672785,0.00266269,0.02510057,0.00525439,-0.01139935,0.06131073,-0.00011851,-0.00939311,-0.04603558,-0.02693848,0.05828317,-0.01843187,0.04420098,-0.09113616,0.0152004,-0.01925102,-0.07700861,-0.06393376,-0.04549289,-0.24552304,-0.04632687,-0.01950329,0.08297513,-0.0428214,-0.05388435,-0.07969531,-0.02827261,0.0349803,-0.01122305,0.0764659,0.01346328,0.07123089,-0.03538359,-0.01588034,-0.00002068,0.02573621,-0.02825642,0.01672317,-0.01450973,-0.01533543,-0.07228763,0.04924086,0.00311771,0.05150128,0.00479567,0.03801616,0.05875479,0.02333505,0.03817489,0.06801446,0.04183363,0.03318418,-0.15874659,0.03981125,0.05043983,0.03238049,0.00721942,-0.02670793,0.02901319,0.01907414,-0.04346573,0.02777689,0.03399239,0.08947627,0.03632407,-0.04498808,-0.05387633,-0.04219898,0.00433104,0.03437772,-0.01177415,-0.07979435,0.00730463,0.05066268,-0.01463688,-0.01469356,0.01856348,0.01665265,0.06642441,0.01743196,-0.03115701,0.03222534,-0.0095987,0.04756087,0.02193304,0.0233698,0.06070678,-0.00046913,-0.06402808,0.13289107,-0.04789227,0.00471898,0.00383029,0.02213681,0.06628077,-0.01528822,-0.0140571,-0.03640561,-0.08044046,-0.09683134,0.05574708,-0.05209865,0.0289429,-0.0601982,-0.00527932,-0.05992565,0.05892286,0.00110333,0.01942639,-0.00471019,-0.01562038,0.05