"smart_blocks:Computer Science/C++/C++ - Random number generation.md#BBFABBA6;\">object that produces a sequence of uniformly distributed raw random integer values</mark>. It's a stateful object; each time you call it, it generates the next number in its sequence and updates its internal state. The quality and performance of engines vary. A common and good general-purpose choice is the Mersenne Twister (std::mt19937).": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.07331414,-0.00240062,-0.05329641,-0.05787155,-0.03442521,0.02933719,-0.04393081,0.03155709,0.04258699,0.05119763,0.0273613,-0.05018397,-0.01497773,-0.00865291,-0.03325571,-0.00012781,-0.055552,0.00178247,-0.06645937,-0.06665295,0.07347575,-0.02538335,-0.00893096,-0.10571422,-0.02065772,-0.02010657,-0.05432436,-0.01571805,-0.07693882,-0.24221498,-0.00484289,-0.01676563,0.06589978,-0.0495721,-0.06013745,-0.08191185,-0.04268982,0.04351044,-0.05080079,0.09515022,0.00699659,0.09343996,-0.02105889,-0.03096595,-0.02257638,-0.01619804,-0.02506871,0.04049569,0.05742691,0.01829336,-0.07420097,0.03220286,0.00159583,0.03674407,0.03621551,0.01956484,0.03868603,0.04112695,-0.01195516,0.04559407,0.05495828,0.02724422,-0.14305733,0.07020029,0.0196661,0.04514393,0.0007025,-0.08392744,0.00522862,0.01694106,0.01202726,-0.01094079,0.03671967,0.07669967,0.05567932,-0.0672581,-0.07374252,-0.03899491,-0.00489093,0.06665322,-0.0388529,-0.05068482,-0.00069194,0.05812109,-0.01471051,-0.00762114,0.00328499,-0.02864538,0.10574703,0.04147686,-0.04357669,0.03615059,-0.0312165,0.04188089,0.01494689,0.01918812,0.08641864,0.03345422,-0.00806068,0.10446743,-0.04364177,-0.0052811,0.01856575,-0.01016978,0.03826386,0.00307851,-0.04419865,-0.03975604,-0.10346478,-0.05375426,0.06055183,-0.01188926,0.02452166,-0.08795368,-0.04985668,-0.03702928,0.04498799,-0.003009,0.00716258,-0.05120463,-0.00380291,0.09552906,0.01316258,0.02010541,0.04499133,0.01817182,0.02025083,0.0710407,-0.00018913,0.046501,0.05618977,0.04113812,-0.06825635,