"smart_blocks:Computer Science/C++/C++ - Random number generation.md#D2B3FFA6;\">An engine must be \"seeded\" to start its sequence at an unpredictable point</mark>. If you seed two engines with the same value, they will produce the exact same sequence of numbers. For non-deterministic seeding, std::random_device is used. It's a source of true non-deterministic randomness (if supported by the hardware/OS) used to seed a more performant engine like mt19937.": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.04661082,-0.00847343,-0.06747238,-0.02159822,-0.02096007,0.0235255,-0.08142781,0.010957,0.05467873,0.02052097,0.02934195,-0.02664999,0.0310512,-0.00272483,-0.01407168,0.03017025,-0.05975579,0.03698071,-0.05016524,-0.02309147,0.08944447,-0.0503261,0.01348663,-0.13952558,-0.00224003,-0.00676987,-0.05319455,-0.02863111,-0.02246748,-0.24960551,0.00832342,0.03354878,0.03257075,-0.04589137,-0.04151433,-0.05796834,-0.04845444,0.06639612,-0.04363309,0.07809097,0.02369392,0.06071185,-0.07195386,-0.01695979,-0.00021439,-0.00092657,-0.02773561,0.03107291,0.02693663,-0.01776732,-0.05132765,0.04501176,0.01715247,0.00889278,0.01412228,-0.01555102,0.05532366,0.0640863,-0.01440716,0.04418518,-0.00328085,0.01957639,-0.15167539,0.04827574,0.00888335,0.01562679,0.00295117,-0.04102539,0.03192087,0.01340672,0.03057237,-0.00406077,0.01624459,0.07034414,0.03707786,-0.06751561,-0.04922454,0.00098366,-0.01886735,0.04538019,-0.03174014,-0.03768841,-0.04415993,0.05205691,-0.04651521,0.00739413,0.02750682,-0.01244639,0.08842537,0.00854044,-0.05040162,0.03200414,-0.05231203,0.03264159,0.05381868,0.04853357,0.05380296,-0.04405706,-0.00938117,0.09092395,0.00470986,0.00438736,0.00548053,0.03004645,0.0284904,0.00268498,-0.07408118,-0.06666984,-0.05851299,-0.06862924,0.06639531,-0.03718378,0.03774128,-0.08933534,-0.00715464,-0.06218133,0.00371159,-0.00482251,-0.00127424,-0.05024733,-0.01658308,0.09893092,0.02792632,-0.0041671,0.05812679,-0.00816534,0.0245501,0.07039896,0.01440217,0.04